<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stolpen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stolpen is a small town east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dresden">Dresden</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, crowned by a castle on a basalt hill. It was a residence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meissen">Meissen</a> until 1559, when it passed to the Electorate of Saxony, and Augustus the Strong's former mistress Countess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kozle">Cosel</a> was confined there from 1716 until her death in 1765.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stolpen.jpg" alt="Stolpen" width="320" height="197" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hagar66 based on work of TUBS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stolpen_in_PIR.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
